{
  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_002: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200 → 52.0% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether image information carries useful signal at all. Without an image-only baseline, any future multimodal result cannot be attributed to fusion benefit vs. mere addition of a second modality. config_041 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) directly complements the existing rna_only baseline by matching the profile setting (singleprofile) and using the strongest available image encoder, cleanly isolating the modality effect. This is the highest-information experiment under the current sparse evidence: if image accuracy is low, multimodal gains will likely be modest and RNA-centric; if it is competitive, fusion strategy and encoder choice become the key levers to explore next."
}

